# Add a picture

Put a photograph, drawing or diagram in a chapter.

1. In the editor, put the cursor on an empty line where the picture should go, with a blank line above it.
2. Drag the picture file from your computer onto the editor.
3. A line like `![lighthouse](../Images/lighthouse.png)` appears. The word in square brackets is selected: type a short description of the picture to replace it.

``` djot
![The lighthouse at dusk, its lamp lit.](../Images/lighthouse.png)
```

The preview shows the picture as soon as you drop it.

The description is read aloud to readers who cannot see the picture, and shown if the picture cannot load. Say what the picture shows, in a sentence.

To use the same picture again, choose [Images]{.ui} from the [Insert]{.ui} list above the editor, put the cursor where you want it, and click the picture.

Use JPEG or PNG files for photographs and drawings, and SVG for diagrams. Every reading app can show them.
